{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:6dbce61dff72c8e6","name":"Pherin","source":{"id":"source:reference-6dbce61dff72c8e6","title":"Pherin","revision":21229,"timestamp":"2024-08-26T01:23:54Z","sha256":"945ec695bf9bfe4470ac70e1c73d7fdd737da9924e8cab31fb334cb718218e46","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=21229","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Pherin&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-6dbce61dff72c8e6","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Galaxy of Intrigue"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Galaxy_of_Intrigue"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["The creature is ",{"tag":"a","children":["Human"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Human","referenceId":"reference:9ffa865f2bc6e850"},"-sized, but its form is distinctly alien. Long, spindly limbs with large, knobby joints protrude from its body at seemingly random angles. Its wide head is squat with two bulbous eyes that look about independently. A series of blue-green spots produce a dim glow along the creature's abdomen."]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Pherins are omnivores of medium size. They are as close to being genuinely sentient as any other species native to ",{"tag":"a","children":["Nyriaan"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Nyriaan","referenceId":"reference:ffb4373927de3433"},". A Pherin is froglike, with four spindly limbs, knobby joints, bulbous eyes, and a wide, tooth-lined mouth. Two or more Pherin families might travel alongside a herd of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Lluma"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Lluma","referenceId":"reference:26e1e3aaab6dcab8"},", competing- and occasionally feuding- with other groups of Pherin for resources and food.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Pherins have been known to use rudimentary tools, including improvised melee weapons and thrown stones. They are curious to a fault, and many meet violent ends after wandering into a prospecting town or other settlement. Like the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Lluma"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Lluma","referenceId":"reference:26e1e3aaab6dcab8"}," they follow, Pherins can assume one of three genders, seemingly at will. Family units consist of equal numbers of males and females, with neuters making up between ten and twenty percent of the population.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Pherin Tactics"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Pherins attack en masse, disabling targets that seem dangerous or especially intimidating before moving on to less-capable prey. Although they are peaceful and rarely attack unless provoked, they are nonetheless capable of spontaneous violence if given the opportunity. Male Pherins are more likely to attack than females, with neuters being especially aggressive if their family unit is threatened.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Pherin Statistics (CL 3)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Normal"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Medium ",{"tag":"a","children":["Beast"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Beast","referenceId":"reference:628bf77a740094a9"}," 4\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +4; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Darkvision"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Darkvision"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +4\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},": 14 (",{"tag":"a","children":["Flat-Footed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Flat-Footed"},": 12), ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortitude Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fortitude_Defense"},": 11, ",{"tag